         "title": "Foreign tourists in Japan eat far more rice than previously thought, according to new data",
         "description": "The average overseas visitor now consumes more rice in a day than a Japanese local. On 27 July, Japan’s Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (MAFF) released its fiscal 2025 data on rice consumption by foreign visitors to Japan, and the results revealed that foreign tourists are eating significantly more rice than anticipated. According to [\u0026#8230;]",
         "content": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-740673\" src=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?w=640\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"472\" srcset=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg 1600w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=150,111 150w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=640,472 640w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=768,566 768w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=1024,755 1024w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=1536,1133 1536w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=95,70 95w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=190,140 190w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=285,210 285w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=133,98 133w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=266,196 266w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-1.jpeg?resize=399,294 399w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-size: large\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe average overseas visitor now consumes more rice in a day than a Japanese local.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan id=\"more-740659\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn 27 July, Japan’s Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (MAFF) released its\u003cstrong\u003e fiscal 2025 data on rice consumption by foreign visitors to Japan\u003c/strong\u003e, and the results revealed that\u003cstrong\u003e foreign tourists are eating significantly more rice than anticipated\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to the data, collected through questionnaires completed by \u003cstrong\u003evisitors from 14 countries and regions\u003c/strong\u003e, MAFF now estimates that overseas visitors consume an average of \u003cstrong\u003e570 grams (20 ounces) of cooked rice per day \u003c/strong\u003eduring their stay in Japan, which is roughly the equivalent of four standard bowls of rice.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style=\"text-align: center\"\u003e▼ This is a significant increase from its previous estimate of around 350 grams, or about 2.5 bowls, per person per day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-740680\" src=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-11.jpeg?w=640\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"426\" srcset=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-11.jpeg 1600w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-11.jpeg?resize=150,100 150w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-11.jpeg?resize=640,426 640w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-11.jpeg?resize=768,512 768w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-11.jpeg?resize=1024,682 1024w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-11.jpeg?resize=1536,1023 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTopping the list for rice consumption was \u003cstrong\u003eVietnam\u003c/strong\u003e, at 718 grams, followed by \u003cstrong\u003eIndonesia\u003c/strong\u003e (714 grams), the \u003cstrong\u003ePhilippines\u003c/strong\u003e (695 grams), and \u003cstrong\u003eThailand\u003c/strong\u003e (629 grams). Visitors from the \u003cstrong\u003eU.S.\u003c/strong\u003e consumed an average of 565 grams, while those from \u003cstrong\u003eChina\u003c/strong\u003e consumed 546 grams. The lowest average among the surveyed groups was \u003cstrong\u003eHong Kong\u003c/strong\u003e, whose visitors still consumed 468 grams.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-740679\" src=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-10.jpeg?w=640\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"427\" srcset=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-10.jpeg 1600w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-10.jpeg?resize=150,100 150w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-10.jpeg?resize=640,427 640w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-10.jpeg?resize=768,512 768w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-10.jpeg?resize=1024,683 1024w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-10.jpeg?resize=1536,1024 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo put these figures into perspective, the average person in Japan is said to consume roughly 330–340 grams of cooked rice a day. That means the average foreign visitor eats around 70 percent more rice for each day of their stay than the average Japanese resident.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-740681\" src=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-15.jpeg?w=640\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"426\" srcset=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-15.jpeg 1600w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-15.jpeg?resize=150,100 150w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-15.jpeg?resize=640,426 640w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-15.jpeg?resize=768,512 768w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-15.jpeg?resize=1024,682 1024w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-15.jpeg?resize=1536,1023 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMAFF says the higher figures are linked not only to \u003cstrong\u003emeals at sushi restaurants\u003c/strong\u003e but also to the popularity of \u003cstrong\u003eonigiri rice balls\u003c/strong\u003e, with many tourists enjoying rice multiple times throughout the day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-740678\" src=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-9.jpeg?w=640\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"426\" srcset=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-9.jpeg 1600w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-9.jpeg?resize=150,100 150w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-9.jpeg?resize=640,426 640w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-9.jpeg?resize=768,512 768w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-9.jpeg?resize=1024,682 1024w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-9.jpeg?resize=1536,1023 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJapanese locals, on the other hand, are more likely to add other carbohydrate sources to their daily diets, largely in the form of bread and noodles, in addition to their everyday rice consumption.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style=\"text-align: center\"\u003e▼ Of course, burgers are now part of the diet too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-740674\" src=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-2.jpeg?w=640\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"426\" srcset=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-2.jpeg 1600w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-2.jpeg?resize=150,100 150w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-2.jpeg?resize=640,426 640w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-2.jpeg?resize=768,512 768w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-2.jpeg?resize=1024,682 1024w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-2.jpeg?resize=1536,1023 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy the ministry\u0026#8217;s latest calculations, foreign visitors are estimated to have consumed approximately 82,000 tonnes of polished rice, equivalent to 91,000 tonnes of brown rice, between July 2025 and June 2026. This is a substantial upward revision from the previous estimate of 61,000 tonnes in March of this year.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe updated estimate comes in the wake of Japan’s 2024 rice shortage, dubbed the “Reiwa Rice Riots”, when soaring prices and empty shelves caused concern across the country. While poor harvests linked to extreme heat were a major factor, record numbers of foreign visitors that year also raised questions about whether tourism demand had been underestimated.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-740676\" src=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-4.jpeg?w=640\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"427\" srcset=\"https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-4.jpeg 1600w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-4.jpeg?resize=150,100 150w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-4.jpeg?resize=640,427 640w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-4.jpeg?resize=768,512 768w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-4.jpeg?resize=1024,683 1024w, https://soranews24.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Foreign-tourists-eat-rice-in-Japan-food-forecast-international-visitors-consumption-Reiwa-riots-shortage-supply-demand-government-tourism-boom-sushi-onigiri-travel-news-4.jpeg?resize=1536,1024 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollowing the shortage, the government decided to look into foreign visitor consumption, as it was something that hadn’t previously been considered. By including the rice-eating habits of visitors, these latest figures now provide a more comprehensive account from which to properly assess supply and demand and better prepare the industry for possible changes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhether this leads to increased rice production remains to be seen, as factors such as small farm sizes, an ageing, dwindling workforce, and longstanding policies designed to control rice production still have a strong hold on the industry.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, the government has expressed a willingness to move away from some of the older supply-control measures to effectively meet modern demands. With inbound tourism now being taken into consideration, here\u0026#8217;s hoping future forecasts better reflect the reality of the situation so measures can be put in place to deal with any potential shortages ahead of time and prevent a recurrence of the \u003ca href=\"https://soranews24.com/2024/08/22/foreign-tourists-blamed-for-japan-rice-shortage-as-reiwa-rice-riots-leaves-shelves-bare/\"\u003eReiwa Rice Riots\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eSource: \u003ca href=\"https://www.maff.go.jp/j/tokei/kouhyou/zyukyu/index.html\"\u003eMinistry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries\u003c/a\u003e via \u003ca href=\"https://news.yahoo.co.jp/articles/f5a654dd7555464cde8d673336780d2bd6077fc2\"\u003eYahoo! News Japan/Kyodo\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003c/em\u003e\u003cem\u003eTop image: \u003ca href=\"https://www.pakutaso.com/20141235344post-4928.html\"\u003ePakutaso\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cem\u003eInsert images: Pakutaso (\u003ca href=\"https://www.pakutaso.com/20170516138post-11558.html\"\u003e1\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://www.pakutaso.com/20201228359post-32628.html\"\u003e2\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://www.pakutaso.com/20120304065post-1255.html\"\u003e3\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://www.pakutaso.com/20170601158tl.html\"\u003e4\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://www.pakutaso.com/20190818226post-22647.html\"\u003e5\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://www.pakutaso.com/20240722187post-51670.html\"\u003e6\u003c/a\u003e)\u003c/em\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cem\u003e● Want to hear about SoraNews24\u0026#8217;s latest articles as soon as they\u0026#8217;re published? \u003ca href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RocketNews24En\"\u003eFollow us on Facebook\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://twitter.com/RocketNews24En\"\u003eTwitter\u003c/a\u003e!\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
